<title>USA: Motorola makes management changes.</title>
<headline>Motorola makes management changes.</headline>
<dateline>SCHAUMBURG, Ill. 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Motorola Inc said Monday that Edward Staiano will retire as president of its General Systems Sector to become vice chairman and chief executive offier of Iridium LLC, effective January 1.</p>
<p>Also, Jack Scanlon, general manager of the Cellular Infrastructure Group, will become president and general manager of the new Cellular Natworks and Space Sector.</p>
<p>Motorola also named Robert Weisshappel general manager of its Cellular Subscriber Group.</p>
<p>The company makes cellular equipment and semiconductors.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
